WEBVTT

00:00:01.253 --> 00:00:06.123
Yume kara samete mo
Even if I wake from my dreams

00:00:07.163 --> 00:00:12.623
Kono te wo nobasu yo
I'll reach my hand out to you

00:00:24.143 --> 00:00:29.413
Onaji tsuyosa de yobi au
If our hearts can reach each other

00:00:30.153 --> 00:00:34.783
Kokoro ni nareru no naraba
with the same strength

00:00:36.023 --> 00:00:41.293
Nanninbun no kizu demo
Then I would be able to bare

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:46.963
Boku wa uketome rareru yo
The pain of many hearts

00:00:47.373 --> 00:00:50.963
Mousukoshi datte kiga surun da
I can feel that it will arrive soon

00:00:51.043 --> 00:00:55.913
Kono kabe ga kuzureru
When these walls will be torn down

00:00:56.713 --> 00:01:01.113
Reimei
The dawn

00:01:02.853 --> 00:01:08.813
Yume kara samete mo
mada minai yume no houmade
Even if we wake from our dreams
We'll have to keep running

00:01:08.893 --> 00:01:14.793
Bokura wa hitori de
hashiri tuzukeru shika nain da
Towards our unrevealed dreams

00:01:14.863 --> 00:01:21.433
Korogari mayotte tsukuri dasu
boku no inryoku ga
The gravity by my painful journey
will draw me

00:01:21.703 --> 00:01:27.643
Itsuka kimi e
To you one day

00:02:08.883 --> 00:02:11.253
I never knew
a place like this existed!

00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:15.343
This place is called
"Lost Ground".

00:02:15.893 --> 00:02:18.863
Like, a place
people couldn't find?

00:02:18.993 --> 00:02:19.483
That's right.

00:02:29.073 --> 00:02:30.133
I've kept you waiting.

00:02:30.573 --> 00:02:32.373
Just a little.

00:02:32.543 --> 00:02:33.703
Nice to meet you!

00:02:35.413 --> 00:02:36.673
So, you're Tabby.

00:02:38.983 --> 00:02:40.813
I'm much obliged!

00:02:41.953 --> 00:02:43.073
What should we do?

00:02:43.953 --> 00:02:45.543
Let's go home.

00:02:45.923 --> 00:02:47.853
You've never seen it, have you?

00:02:48.723 --> 00:02:52.183
By "home" do you mean
a place exclusively for the guild?

00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:53.163
That's right.

00:02:53.233 --> 00:02:54.923
Well, let's go home then.

00:02:55.933 --> 00:02:56.363
What about you?

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.003
I'm going to go to him.

00:02:59.433 --> 00:03:00.163
Him?

00:03:00.773 --> 00:03:02.603
There's another candidate.

00:03:03.173 --> 00:03:04.143
Oh.

00:03:24.663 --> 00:03:26.523
So, you did come.

00:03:35.333 --> 00:03:36.733
Let's go for a walk.

00:03:37.243 --> 00:03:38.033
Why?

00:03:38.243 --> 00:03:39.473
Do I need a reason?

00:03:44.813 --> 00:03:45.783
I guess not.

00:03:47.313 --> 00:03:48.613
Then, let's go.

00:03:55.093 --> 00:03:56.023
Aren't you coming?

00:03:59.193 --> 00:04:02.633
Don't worry,
you can't get PK'd in town.

00:04:03.263 --> 00:04:04.563
It's not that.

00:04:12.673 --> 00:04:14.573
Why'd you start playing again?

00:04:15.213 --> 00:04:16.203
Why?

00:04:16.583 --> 00:04:20.273
After what you said,
I didn't think you'd come back.

00:04:20.483 --> 00:04:21.453
That doesn't matter.

00:04:23.083 --> 00:04:24.783
But it does.

00:04:26.523 --> 00:04:28.323
I really don't understand.

00:04:28.753 --> 00:04:30.783
You have a gift.

00:04:32.063 --> 00:04:33.553
What did you say?

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:34.893
A gift.

00:04:36.003 --> 00:04:37.393
Ovan said so, too.

00:04:38.233 --> 00:04:39.753
Hey, you...

00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:41.093
What's your relationship
with Ovan?

00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:43.573
It's more than just being
in the same guild, right?

00:04:43.643 --> 00:04:44.473
Hey...

00:04:44.703 --> 00:04:46.303
It's not "You".

00:04:47.743 --> 00:04:49.173
It's Shino.

00:04:51.743 --> 00:04:52.643
Shino...

00:04:53.453 --> 00:04:54.713
Hey, Haseo?

00:04:55.783 --> 00:04:57.083
Would you like to come with us?

00:04:57.583 --> 00:05:00.713
You haven't joined a guild
yet, right?

00:05:02.023 --> 00:05:03.353
Hello?

00:05:03.693 --> 00:05:04.623
First...

00:05:04.693 --> 00:05:05.683
What?

00:05:05.763 --> 00:05:07.563
Answer my question.

00:05:08.763 --> 00:05:10.893
You mean about our relationship?

00:05:11.703 --> 00:05:16.793
When Ovan isn't around
I stand in as the master.

00:05:17.173 --> 00:05:18.933
Maybe we've become
a little similar.

00:05:20.013 --> 00:05:21.203
What kind of guild is it?

00:05:21.373 --> 00:05:22.773
The "Twilight Brigade".

00:05:23.013 --> 00:05:24.203
Have you heard of it?

00:05:25.683 --> 00:05:27.243
I heard you're
looking for something.

00:05:28.313 --> 00:05:30.343
The "Key of the Twilight".

00:05:32.253 --> 00:05:33.953
But that's not all.

00:05:36.923 --> 00:05:40.693
Well, aren't you going to
answer my question?

00:05:41.763 --> 00:05:43.823
You don't have to answer
right away.

00:05:45.433 --> 00:05:46.233
Where's Ovan?

00:05:46.873 --> 00:05:47.463
Right now?

00:05:47.873 --> 00:05:49.963
He's with a new member
that just joined.

00:05:50.043 --> 00:05:51.003
New?

00:05:51.473 --> 00:05:53.843
Yes, I invited her.

00:05:57.183 --> 00:05:58.013
I pass.

00:05:58.643 --> 00:05:59.513
On the guild.

00:06:00.253 --> 00:06:01.113
I see.

00:06:02.253 --> 00:06:03.313
Oh, well.

00:06:03.483 --> 00:06:04.453
I understand.

00:06:04.753 --> 00:06:05.613
I...

00:06:05.753 --> 00:06:09.483
We need you.
But, I won't force you to join.

00:06:09.923 --> 00:06:12.193
Here. It's my
member address.

00:06:14.063 --> 00:06:15.293
It's a registered one.

00:06:15.803 --> 00:06:17.423
Contact me if you need to.

00:06:20.433 --> 00:06:21.593
Oh, and...

00:06:22.903 --> 00:06:24.633
When you're talking to someone...

00:06:24.703 --> 00:06:25.973
...you should look them in the eye.

00:06:27.673 --> 00:06:28.733
In the eye?

00:06:29.983 --> 00:06:31.743
But this is a game.

00:06:32.343 --> 00:06:34.783
Why bother looking a CG
in the eye?

00:06:34.913 --> 00:06:36.383
So what if it's a game?

00:06:36.453 --> 00:06:38.973
You should do it precisely
because it is a game.

00:06:39.253 --> 00:06:42.223
You don't want to talk to
someone who's looking the other way.

00:06:42.963 --> 00:06:44.453
I don't get it.

00:06:44.863 --> 00:06:46.293
You know, with babies...

00:06:46.763 --> 00:06:50.893
...they can't talk, so they watch
their mother's face very closely.

00:06:52.333 --> 00:06:55.863
Can't you do something
even a baby can do?

00:06:58.243 --> 00:06:59.203
Well, good-bye!

00:07:05.283 --> 00:07:06.903
It's been awhile!

00:07:07.583 --> 00:07:09.783
I've been here the whole time.

00:07:15.453 --> 00:07:17.353
It's like a secret base!

00:07:18.863 --> 00:07:19.853
A new member?

00:07:20.493 --> 00:07:20.893
Yes.

00:07:21.133 --> 00:07:21.993
That's Tabby.

00:07:22.703 --> 00:07:23.393
Tabby?

00:07:25.603 --> 00:07:26.863
This is Sakisaka.

00:07:26.933 --> 00:07:29.563
I'm going to put you two together
for a while.

00:07:32.343 --> 00:07:34.643
Nice to meet you.
It's a pleasure.

00:07:35.113 --> 00:07:37.233
Yeah, yeah, nice to meet you.

00:07:37.713 --> 00:07:39.743
So, are you taking off again?

00:07:40.113 --> 00:07:41.443
To gather information.

00:07:41.813 --> 00:07:44.753
Well, I guess it doesn't matter
if you're not around.

00:07:44.823 --> 00:07:47.813
We're getting more members,
so we can probably make do.

00:07:48.493 --> 00:07:49.323
Sorry.

00:07:51.463 --> 00:07:52.793
It's Tabby, right?

00:07:53.663 --> 00:07:54.153
Yes?

00:07:54.463 --> 00:07:55.453
What level...

00:07:55.533 --> 00:07:57.363
Wait, don't tell me
you just started?

00:07:57.463 --> 00:07:59.993
I'm a bright and eager beginner!

00:08:00.073 --> 00:08:01.593
Thanks for taking me
under your wing!

00:08:01.673 --> 00:08:03.603
Oh, what am I going to do?

00:08:11.213 --> 00:08:12.513
What do you want to know?

00:08:12.583 --> 00:08:13.703
About the Brigade.

00:08:14.053 --> 00:08:15.713
You declined, didn't you?

00:08:16.853 --> 00:08:18.543
Yeah, but...

00:08:18.723 --> 00:08:21.383
Well, okay.
I don't know much, though.

00:08:21.853 --> 00:08:24.253
So, what's it about?

00:08:24.893 --> 00:08:27.123
The Key of the Twilight.

00:08:28.733 --> 00:08:33.963
A legendary item that once
existed in The World.

00:08:34.573 --> 00:08:37.133
The Twilight Brigade
is searching for it.

00:08:38.003 --> 00:08:38.903
Legendary?

00:08:40.013 --> 00:08:42.943
It's all written in the forum.

00:08:46.213 --> 00:08:47.343
I'm going to go look.

00:08:47.413 --> 00:08:49.473
No, you don't need to do that.

00:08:49.883 --> 00:08:52.483
No matter what, in the end
it's all speculation.

00:08:53.323 --> 00:08:57.453
It just says that it exists,
but nobody knows what it's for.

00:09:00.263 --> 00:09:03.493
Like whether your whole status
is raised to the highest level...

00:09:03.563 --> 00:09:05.393
...or you get
more pocket money.

00:09:05.503 --> 00:09:09.463
Or you get a weapon that's
one of a kind in this game...

00:09:09.543 --> 00:09:12.333
...or have fulfilled
any wish you may desire.

00:09:12.403 --> 00:09:13.373
That's enough.

00:09:14.573 --> 00:09:19.243
Some say it can override some
basic principles of the game rules.

00:09:19.353 --> 00:09:23.783
If the rules can be overridden
the game will fall apart.

00:09:24.223 --> 00:09:25.183
That kind of thing...

00:09:26.093 --> 00:09:27.713
There's no such thing.

00:09:28.993 --> 00:09:33.293
But, the Twilight Brigade thinks
there is and is looking for it.

00:09:36.463 --> 00:09:40.193
If it's a guild, it must have
quite a few members, right?

00:09:40.533 --> 00:09:42.093
It's a small guild.

00:09:42.533 --> 00:09:44.263
There's just a few of them.

00:09:44.343 --> 00:09:45.463
Yeah, but still.

00:09:45.543 --> 00:09:47.303
Does everyone believe it?

00:09:47.413 --> 00:09:51.373
Who knows?
Maybe they're just curious.

00:09:52.113 --> 00:09:55.413
That strange Ovan is
the Guild Master, after all.

00:09:56.683 --> 00:09:57.913
Would you like to meet him?

00:09:59.053 --> 00:09:59.923
Meet Ovan?

00:10:00.593 --> 00:10:02.923
I know someone
who used to be a member.

00:10:03.123 --> 00:10:04.053
Used to be?

00:10:05.393 --> 00:10:07.523
She happens to be online
right now.

00:10:07.593 --> 00:10:10.533
Whether or not she'll talk to you
is another matter.

00:10:10.633 --> 00:10:13.333
If that's okay with you,
I'll introduce you.

00:10:26.813 --> 00:10:28.443
You've made over 40 hits!

00:10:30.123 --> 00:10:31.643
Um... Um...

00:10:39.223 --> 00:10:41.023
You're leading this, Tabby.

00:10:41.093 --> 00:10:43.433
You've got the Rengeki trigger.

00:10:43.503 --> 00:10:44.483
You're good to go.

00:10:44.903 --> 00:10:45.733
Okay!

00:10:46.333 --> 00:10:48.423
Okay, Sakisaka! I'm going for it!

00:10:54.143 --> 00:10:55.543
Amazing!

00:10:55.743 --> 00:10:57.943
That attack was so powerful!

00:10:58.013 --> 00:11:01.713
You see? If you use it effectively
your level will soar up.

00:11:01.913 --> 00:11:04.513
But I can't do this by
myself, right?

00:11:05.353 --> 00:11:07.323
Well, I guess not.

00:11:08.793 --> 00:11:10.523
Thanks for being my partner!

00:11:11.223 --> 00:11:12.023
Who me?

00:11:12.463 --> 00:11:15.153
You know how to use
spells, right?

00:11:15.293 --> 00:11:18.993
And Ovan's so strong he'll
defeat them without my help.

00:11:19.903 --> 00:11:21.763
So you're the only one.

00:11:22.673 --> 00:11:23.833
I guess I have no choice.

00:11:29.583 --> 00:11:30.973
You're late.

00:11:36.123 --> 00:11:37.553
Phyllo told me.

00:11:37.983 --> 00:11:38.783
Come here.

00:11:41.893 --> 00:11:42.953
Uh, right...

00:11:55.773 --> 00:11:57.263
How far are we going?

00:11:57.343 --> 00:11:58.773
Just follow me.

00:12:01.273 --> 00:12:02.803
I don't want anyone else to hear...

00:12:04.413 --> 00:12:06.213
...that I was in that guild.

00:12:14.093 --> 00:12:15.253
Here's fine.

00:12:16.323 --> 00:12:18.953
I hear you want to know
why I left.

00:12:19.963 --> 00:12:23.493
Something must be happening
with the Twilight Brigade...

00:12:23.633 --> 00:12:25.153
...if it has the old man talking.

00:12:25.233 --> 00:12:26.293
No, not yet.

00:12:28.633 --> 00:12:30.033
Whatever.

00:12:30.343 --> 00:12:33.363
You're better off
staying clear of that guild.

00:12:34.013 --> 00:12:35.173
"That guild"?

00:12:35.613 --> 00:12:37.403
Didn't they do lots for you?

00:12:37.483 --> 00:12:38.413
Do lots for me?

00:12:39.783 --> 00:12:41.583
I did lots for them.

00:12:44.053 --> 00:12:47.313
Because of this thing called
the "Key of the Twilight"...

00:12:47.423 --> 00:12:49.943
...I was sent to all kinds of
strange, stupid areas...

00:12:50.363 --> 00:12:53.693
...and had to be on standby
in those areas for hours on end.

00:12:53.833 --> 00:12:56.593
If you weren't being forced,
why didn't you just leave?

00:12:57.663 --> 00:13:00.793
You were there voluntarily
and you stuck around...

00:13:00.873 --> 00:13:02.803
...so you must have
believed it existed.

00:13:03.843 --> 00:13:08.503
What did the Key of the Twilight
mean to the Brigade?

00:13:08.913 --> 00:13:10.203
Why were you looking for it?

00:13:10.683 --> 00:13:13.913
To be honest, it wasn't the item
I was interested in.

00:13:16.423 --> 00:13:19.253
Why are you interested
in the Brigade?

00:13:20.993 --> 00:13:22.923
Because of Ovan, I think.

00:13:24.163 --> 00:13:25.253
I see.

00:13:26.023 --> 00:13:27.653
It was the same for me.

00:13:29.133 --> 00:13:30.393
But, you know...

00:13:30.463 --> 00:13:34.163
...even if you join them
you won't understand Ovan.

00:13:34.233 --> 00:13:36.503
I know he's incomprehensible.

00:13:38.103 --> 00:13:39.503
They'll only use you.

00:13:40.013 --> 00:13:40.733
For what?

00:13:41.143 --> 00:13:42.113
Well...

00:13:42.843 --> 00:13:45.243
...actually, there's someone else
who left, too.

00:13:45.683 --> 00:13:46.843
Want to meet him?

00:13:47.013 --> 00:13:47.503
Sure.

00:13:48.753 --> 00:13:49.743
Just wait a little bit.

00:13:53.723 --> 00:13:56.813
He's a bit troublesome,
but he says he'll meet you.

00:13:57.523 --> 00:13:58.323
Troublesome?

00:14:02.833 --> 00:14:03.953
You're a disgrace.

00:14:06.903 --> 00:14:08.993
I'm tired.

00:14:09.073 --> 00:14:11.003
It's your job to stock the place.

00:14:11.073 --> 00:14:12.163
Quit complaining.

00:14:12.243 --> 00:14:15.543
My job in the real world
is enough.

00:14:16.173 --> 00:14:18.443
Hey, where did you get that?

00:14:19.043 --> 00:14:19.573
Huh?

00:14:20.183 --> 00:14:20.773
This?

00:14:21.253 --> 00:14:22.413
I just found it.

00:14:24.183 --> 00:14:26.213
The god of business
is descending!

00:14:30.223 --> 00:14:30.783
What?

00:14:30.863 --> 00:14:33.623
That's the thing
I've been looking for!

00:14:33.863 --> 00:14:35.953
At least let me try it out first.

00:14:36.933 --> 00:14:40.233
Why not!
I'm not in a hurry.

00:14:40.433 --> 00:14:42.463
You can use it for a while.

00:14:42.833 --> 00:14:44.773
You're pretty generous.

00:14:44.903 --> 00:14:45.893
Idiot.

00:14:46.073 --> 00:14:47.773
We'd better keep it a secret
for a while.

00:14:51.113 --> 00:14:54.273
What I really want
is a unique weapon...

00:14:54.353 --> 00:14:57.983
...that only I would possess
in The World.

00:14:58.323 --> 00:15:00.793
Tawaraya, can't you get it for me?

00:15:01.393 --> 00:15:03.053
This sounds interesting.

00:15:03.523 --> 00:15:04.783
What are you talking about?

00:15:05.663 --> 00:15:07.633
The Key of the Twilight.

00:15:09.703 --> 00:15:13.223
No matter who the opponent,
this weapon can defeat them.

00:15:14.103 --> 00:15:16.033
You think it exists?

00:15:16.373 --> 00:15:18.303
No, I don't. I was kidding.

00:15:19.273 --> 00:15:21.403
But Naobi's looking for it.

00:15:21.913 --> 00:15:23.503
Can you really say that
it doesn't exist?

00:15:24.283 --> 00:15:28.243
Naobi's only interested
in what Ovan's interested in.

00:15:28.853 --> 00:15:31.583
There's no smoke
where there's no fire.

00:15:32.283 --> 00:15:36.083
A merchant can make smoke
where there is no fire.

00:15:36.823 --> 00:15:38.263
Oh! Got to get back to work!

00:15:38.493 --> 00:15:40.253
Don't lose that!

00:15:41.063 --> 00:15:41.993
Yeah, yeah.

00:15:44.533 --> 00:15:45.893
So it didn't work.

00:15:46.303 --> 00:15:47.273
You know...

00:15:48.533 --> 00:15:51.373
...I think it would be better
if you went instead of me.

00:15:53.313 --> 00:15:56.103
He's really interested in you.

00:15:56.613 --> 00:15:57.273
I see.

00:15:58.243 --> 00:15:59.043
I don't know.

00:16:01.283 --> 00:16:03.343
Maybe I said too much.

00:16:04.523 --> 00:16:07.583
I didn't mention Tabby's name...

00:16:07.653 --> 00:16:09.213
...but I told him she was with you.

00:16:10.023 --> 00:16:10.993
Oh?

00:16:11.723 --> 00:16:14.563
He's stubborn or something.

00:16:16.333 --> 00:16:18.803
I think it would be best
if you went.

00:16:18.903 --> 00:16:19.663
Okay.

00:16:19.733 --> 00:16:20.723
I'll do that.

00:16:20.873 --> 00:16:22.273
You're awfully agreeable.

00:16:22.373 --> 00:16:24.103
I just felt the same. That's all.

00:16:25.403 --> 00:16:25.963
But...

00:16:28.173 --> 00:16:31.613
I have a feeling Haseo will join.

00:16:32.183 --> 00:16:34.153
Yes, he definitely will.

00:16:35.313 --> 00:16:36.413
How do you know?

00:16:38.953 --> 00:16:39.923
Woman's intuition.

00:17:24.603 --> 00:17:26.723
Well, you passed the test.

00:17:26.803 --> 00:17:29.633
You're weak,
but you have the will to win.

00:17:29.703 --> 00:17:31.333
Who are you?

00:17:32.543 --> 00:17:34.273
You're Haseo, right?

00:17:35.173 --> 00:17:35.873
Yeah.

00:17:36.273 --> 00:17:38.503
Didn't Bset tell you anything?

00:17:38.743 --> 00:17:40.683
She said I'd know
when I got here.

00:17:40.753 --> 00:17:44.043
So, she didn't tell you about me.

00:17:44.983 --> 00:17:47.853
Saving the weak!
Defeating the strong!

00:17:47.923 --> 00:17:48.683
I'm the righteous-

00:17:48.753 --> 00:17:49.723
A PK?

00:17:49.863 --> 00:17:51.983
Well, you could say that.

00:17:52.623 --> 00:17:54.153
So, what are you going to do?

00:17:54.833 --> 00:17:56.423
What do you mean?

00:17:57.133 --> 00:17:59.103
Aren't you going to defeat Ovan?

00:17:59.163 --> 00:17:59.723
What?

00:17:59.973 --> 00:18:02.733
Oh, you just want to
know about him.

00:18:02.803 --> 00:18:03.363
Yeah.

00:18:03.673 --> 00:18:04.503
For now.

00:18:06.343 --> 00:18:07.503
Well, sit down.

00:18:10.513 --> 00:18:13.483
He's no good, you know.

00:18:13.713 --> 00:18:18.153
Just believing that
"thing" exists makes him weird.

00:18:18.523 --> 00:18:21.013
By that "thing", you mean
the Key of the Twilight?

00:18:21.093 --> 00:18:25.353
Yeah. The purpose of a legend
in this world is to be a legend.

00:18:25.593 --> 00:18:29.993
Imagine demons and dragons
popping up all over the real world.

00:18:30.063 --> 00:18:31.593
It just doesn't happen.

00:18:32.903 --> 00:18:34.463
Did you meet Ovan?

00:18:34.933 --> 00:18:35.403
Yeah.

00:18:36.103 --> 00:18:38.403
What did you think
of his left arm?

00:18:38.643 --> 00:18:40.073
What do you mean?

00:18:40.143 --> 00:18:41.773
It looks like cheating to me.

00:18:41.873 --> 00:18:44.213
Normally you can't edit
stuff like that.

00:18:44.283 --> 00:18:45.043
Cheating?

00:18:45.413 --> 00:18:47.113
Illegal action.

00:18:47.283 --> 00:18:49.273
Like tampering with data.

00:18:51.153 --> 00:18:52.983
You'd better stay away from him.

00:18:53.423 --> 00:18:56.353
I have no idea why you're
interested in him

00:18:57.393 --> 00:18:59.983
So, my information fee.

00:19:00.063 --> 00:19:00.623
Huh?

00:19:01.293 --> 00:19:02.823
Give and take.

00:19:03.163 --> 00:19:03.823
Pay up.

00:19:04.633 --> 00:19:07.293
What? I don't have much.

00:19:07.633 --> 00:19:10.473
Then you can pay with your body!

00:19:13.373 --> 00:19:14.343
I'm kidding!

00:19:14.673 --> 00:19:15.643
Just joking.

00:19:16.513 --> 00:19:19.973
This game may not be for you.

00:19:23.683 --> 00:19:24.653
I'm going back.

00:19:37.863 --> 00:19:38.523
Ovan!

00:19:38.903 --> 00:19:40.833
Leveling up by yourself?

00:19:40.903 --> 00:19:41.593
Yeah.

00:19:42.773 --> 00:19:43.463
What about you?

00:19:43.873 --> 00:19:45.273
Waiting for someone.

00:19:46.043 --> 00:19:47.233
Thanks for waiting!

00:19:47.673 --> 00:19:48.163
Oh?

00:19:51.613 --> 00:19:52.703
Do you know him?

00:19:54.113 --> 00:19:55.913
Haseo, let me introduce you.

00:19:56.153 --> 00:19:56.883
This is...

00:19:56.953 --> 00:19:58.213
I'm Tabby!

00:19:58.283 --> 00:20:01.013
I became a member of
the Twilight Brigade today!

00:20:01.093 --> 00:20:02.553
Nice to meet you, Haseo!

00:20:02.993 --> 00:20:05.323
Can I go shopping?

00:20:05.463 --> 00:20:05.953
Sure.

00:20:06.193 --> 00:20:07.753
Okay, I'm off!

00:20:09.763 --> 00:20:11.893
She has a lot of energy.

00:20:14.773 --> 00:20:17.293
Haseo, won't you join me?

00:20:18.773 --> 00:20:20.293
I told you I don't understand.

00:20:21.273 --> 00:20:22.643
Words are inadequate.

00:20:23.943 --> 00:20:26.273
For example,
the Key of the Twilight...

00:20:28.213 --> 00:20:31.413
Talking about it
just raises more questions.

00:20:32.053 --> 00:20:33.023
Does it exist?

00:20:33.353 --> 00:20:35.223
You can decide it's not real.

00:20:35.293 --> 00:20:38.553
Or you can think it might exist
and search for it.

00:20:38.863 --> 00:20:40.693
As a game,
which is more interesting?

00:20:43.963 --> 00:20:45.663
Will you look for it with me?

00:20:47.773 --> 00:20:48.733
I'll think about it.

00:20:50.203 --> 00:20:51.103
That's fine.

00:20:52.173 --> 00:20:53.973
Well, I've got to go.

00:21:15.233 --> 00:21:17.323
It's been awhile.

00:21:18.063 --> 00:21:20.833
You never come to town.

00:21:21.533 --> 00:21:22.333
No, I don't.

00:21:22.903 --> 00:21:25.303
Did you come to see me?

00:21:26.043 --> 00:21:27.733
And if I say yes?

00:21:28.743 --> 00:21:30.473
It's Haseo, isn't it?

00:21:34.853 --> 00:21:36.543
You never change.

00:21:37.453 --> 00:21:39.213
Oh, well. This place won't do.

00:21:39.283 --> 00:21:40.723
Let's go somewhere else.

00:21:40.923 --> 00:21:42.443
Yes, I agree.

00:21:53.973 --> 00:21:58.773
I believe that
Haseo will definitely join us.

00:22:30.273 --> 00:22:33.863
Ikiru wa dokuhai kiyu no kurushimi wo
Life is a poisoned cup of needless suffering

00:22:33.943 --> 00:22:37.373
Nomihosu sube wo dare ga sazukeyo
That no one can show me how to drain

00:22:37.643 --> 00:22:41.373
Taiyo ni sumu toiu kenja no washi
A wise eagle is said to live in the sun

00:22:41.453 --> 00:22:45.473
Habataki dake ga kodama suru
The flapping of its wings
is all that echoes

00:22:48.993 --> 00:22:52.583
Kono futatsu no me ni yadotta
In each of these eyes

00:22:52.663 --> 00:22:56.293
Yami to Hikari sono docchi de
Dwell darkness and light

00:22:56.363 --> 00:23:03.603
Boku wa ashita wo mitsumeru beki nano darou
Through which shall I look to tomorrow?

00:23:03.673 --> 00:23:07.333
Kawaki kitta gareki no machi
A dried out and ruined city

00:23:07.413 --> 00:23:11.103
Ten to sen wo tsunagi awase
Draws the lines between the dots

00:23:11.183 --> 00:23:18.113
Imi nado nai koto bakari afurete iku
Causing meaningless events to overflow

00:23:18.283 --> 00:23:22.013
Honou no gotoki kodoku
Soothing the loneliness

00:23:22.093 --> 00:23:25.113
Idaku karada shizumete wa
That flames up within the body

00:23:25.193 --> 00:23:32.653
Ankyo eto shitatatte iku shizuku
Droplets of water fall towards the culvert

00:23:32.903 --> 00:23:36.093
Kakageru dokuhai kono sei wa michitemo
Even if the poisoned cup is upheld
and filled with this life

00:23:36.173 --> 00:23:40.193
Kogareru shino yume wa nagare tsuku
My dream that yearns for death
drifts into it

00:23:40.313 --> 00:23:43.903
Toride ni kuikomu tsume kokou no washi
The eagle remains aloof;
its talons dig into the fort

00:23:43.983 --> 00:23:47.543
Habataki dake ga maiagaru
Only the flapping of its wings resounds

00:23:47.613 --> 00:23:51.343
Ano soukyu ni takkei ni shite kure tamae
Let me be crucified in the blue sky

00:23:51.423 --> 00:23:54.873
Ten to chi ga musubu basho ni
bokuwa tatsu
I'll stand where heaven and earth meet

00:23:55.923 --> 00:23:57.113
Next Episode...
